  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given nnn sets S1,S2,…,SnS_1, S_2, \\ldots, S_nS1​,S2​,…,Sn​.\n\nFor each iii, you want to choose xi∈Six_i \\in S_ixi​∈Si​, such that the variance of the  multiset {x1,x2,…,xn}\\{x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_n\\}{x1​,x2​,…,xn​} is minimized.\n\nThe variance of a multiset {x1,x2,…,xn}\\{x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_n\\}{x1​,x2​,…,xn​} is defined as σ2=∑i=1n(xi−μ)2n\\sigma^2 = \\displaystyle  \\dfrac{\\sum_{i=1}^{n} (x_i - \\mu)^2}{n} σ2=n∑i=1n​(xi​−μ)2​, where μ\\muμ is the mean, which equals ∑i=1nxin\\displaystyle \\dfrac{ \\sum_{i=1}^{n}x_i}{n}n∑i=1n​xi​​.\n\nSay the minimum possible variance is RRR. Print n2×Rn^2 \\times Rn2×R. It can be proved that n2Rn^2 Rn2R is always an integer.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤n≤50,0001 \\le n \\le 50,0001≤n≤50,000",
      "1≤∣Si∣≤50,000 1 \\le |S_i| \\le 50,0001≤∣Si​∣≤50,000 for all valid iii.",
      "1≤∑i=1n∣Si∣≤50,0001 \\le \\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^{n} |S_i| \\le 50,0001≤i=1∑n​∣Si​∣≤50,000",
      "All elements in a single set are distinct.",
      "The elements of all the sets are between 111 and 50,00050,00050,000 inclusive"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line contains nnn, the number of sets.\nithi^{\\text{th}} ith of the next nnn lines contain an integer ∣Si∣|S_i|∣Si​∣ followed by ∣Si∣|S_i|∣Si​∣ distinct integers denoting the elements of set SiS_iSi​.",
    "outputFormat": "In the only line, print a single integer denoting the product of n2n^2n2 and the minimum possible variance of {x1,x2,…,xn}\\{x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_n\\}{x1​,x2​,…,xn​}",
